# The dynamic symbol table of every published plugin: the symbols the host looks up, and
# nothing else.
#
# Hidden visibility alone does not get there. libstdc++'s headers declare namespace std with
# explicit default visibility, so an out-of-line template member instantiated in a plugin -
# std::vector<std::string>::_M_realloc_insert is the one that shows up first - is exported
# whatever -fvisibility=hidden says, and --exclude-libs cannot reach it because it was
# instantiated in the plugin's own objects rather than pulled from libstdc++.a. Two plugins
# doing that export the same symbol, and the loader binds both to whichever it saw first.
#
# Only defined symbols are affected. The fl_*/rp_* calls a plugin makes stay undefined for the
# host to bind at load, so localising everything here does not touch them.
#
# Two patterns, covering four names. rp_emu_plugin_get and rp_ui_plugin_get are the entry
# points, and a plugin defines exactly one of them; rp_emu_plugin_abi_version is optional and a
# plugin that carries it is asking to be version-checked, so localising it would turn a
# rejection into a silent pass. Patterns rather than names because lld makes an unmatched name
# in `global:` a link error, while an unmatched pattern is allowed.
{
    global:
        rp_*_plugin_get;
        rp_*_plugin_abi_version;
    local:
        *;
};
